From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Asius <dev@asius.ai>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: allow Dragon EL1 boots to reach firmware recovery

Stock Dragon Q6A UEFI initially boots Linux at EL1. Probing the built-in
Venus driver in that mode resets the board in the secure firmware path,
before vamos-hypervisor can request the EL2 override from userspace.

Reject the probe on Dragon when HYP mode is unavailable. This lets the
existing one-shot recovery finish a normal boot and reboot at EL2, where
Venus probes normally. Other boards and the EL2 U-Boot path are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Asius <dev@asius.ai>
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -23,6 +23,10 @@
 #include <media/v4l2-mem2mem.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-ioctl.h>
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_ARM64
+#include <asm/virt.h>
+#endif
+
 #include "core.h"
 #include "firmware.h"
 #include "pm_helpers.h"
@@ -379,6 +383,19 @@
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
 	struct venus_core *core;
 	int ret;
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_ARM64
+	/*
+	 * Stock Dragon UEFI can leave Linux under Gunyah at EL1. Starting
+	 * Venus in that mode resets the SoC before userspace can request the
+	 * firmware's EL2 override. Leave video unavailable for this boot so
+	 * the existing recovery service can complete that transition.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("radxa,dragon-q6a") &&
+	    !is_hyp_mode_available())
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EOPNOTSUPP,
+				     "Dragon Venus requires an EL2 boot; skipping until firmware recovery\n");
+#endif
 
 	core = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*core), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!core)
